x86_64-linux  clang folds this case away where cxx1 emits it: the two file-scope statics the case counts with, Held's constructor and destructor, and the closure's own operator() are all inlined or constant-folded by clang, which emits no symbol for them, while cxx1 emits each as an ordinary definition. That is a difference about emission rather than about naming - the same one lambda.nonames records for a closure and base-implicit-constructor-emitted.nonames for an inline special member. What this case is about, which object a replayed lambda body destroys, is a run-time question and is checked by run.sh on all three machines.
